n":"I do not eat meat and cheese!","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"אתה רוצֶה ארוחת צהריים?","en":"Do you want lunch?","alt":[],"t":"t","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/c57f897b4728a096e474ac11c8b70b1b"},{"he":"אנחנו אוכלים לימון טעים.","en":"We are eating a tasty lemon.","alt":[],"t":"t"},{"he":"ארוחת בוקר או ארוחת צהריים?","en":"Breakfast or lunch?","alt":[],"t":"t"}],"hints":{"דג":"a fish / fish","בשר":"meat / meat, flesh","מלח":"salt","מרק":"soup","סלט":"salad","פרי":"a fruit / fruit","קפה":"coffee","ביצה":"an egg / egg","בירה":"beer","בננה":"a banana / banana","חמאה":"butter","סוכר":"sugar","פסטה":"pasta","צלחת":"a plate / plate, dish","אננס":"pineapple","גבינה":"cheese","לימון":"a lemon / lemon","בא":"come / comes / coming","עגבניה":"a tomato / tomato","זה":"it / it is / it's","אין":"not has / not have / nothing can be done","יש":"I have / do you have / has","ארוחת":"breakfast / lunch","ערב":"evening","זאת":"it is (feminine) / that / that is (feminine)","בוקר":"breakfast / breakfasts / for breakfast","בקבוק":"bottle","מים":"water","טעים":"delicious / tasty / tasty (masculine singular)","אתן":"you (feminine plural) / I will give, allow","אוכלות":"are eating / eat / eating","לה":"her / it (feminine nouns) / she has","לי":"I have / for me / me","כריך":"a sandwich / sandwich","לכם":"do you have / to you (masculine plural) / you","בקר":"beef / visit! (masculine singular)","צהריים":"lunch / noon","טעימה":"tasty (feminine singular)","לא":"aren't / didn't / do not","עגבניות":"tomato","אני":"I / I am / I am a girl","אוכל":"eat / eating / eats","הם":"are / they / they are","רוצים":"do you want / want / want (masculine plural)","להן":"to them / they (feminine)","טעימים":"are delicious / are tasty / tasty (masculine plural)","אבא":"dad / father / father, dad","רוצֶה":"want / wants / would like","רוצָה":"want / wants / would like","שותֶה":"drink / drinking / drinks","אתה":"you / you are / you (masculine singular)","שמן":"oil / fat, chubby","הוא":"(he) is / (it) is / he","הילדה":"the girl / the girl is","הן":"are / they / they are","רוצות":"want (feminine plural)","תפוז":"an orange / orange / orange (fruit)","או":"or","הזיתים":"Mount of olives","אוהב":"like / likes / love","אוהבת":"like / likes / love","את":"it / that / the fruit","היא":"her / it / she","אוכלת":"are eating / eating / is eating","לכן":"that's why / therefore / you","שוקולד":"chocolate","בבקשה":"here you go / please / you are welcome","אתם":"do you want / you / you are","אוכלים":"are eating / eat / eating","תפוח":"an apple / apple","תודה":"thank you / thanks","להם":"them / they do not have / to them","הבשר":"the flesh / the meat","זיתים":"olive","פטרייה":"mushroom","פיצה":"pizza","סליחה":"I am sorry / pardon / excuse me","האוכל":"the food","רואָה":"is seeing / see / sees","האם":"do / does / is","תות":"strawberry","הקפה":"the coffee / the coffee is","לאכול":"eat / eating / to eat","גדול":"big","הפירות":"the fruit","פירות":"fruit","מיץ":"a glass of juice / juice","יין":"wine","ואני":"and I / and I am","רעב":"hungry (masculine singular)","אנחנו":"we / we are / we (plural)"},"words":[{"he":"אתה","en":"you","alt":["you are"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"atah"},{"he":"רוצים","en":"want","alt":["do you want"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"rotzim"},{"he":"הן","en":"are","alt":["they","they are"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"hen"},{"he":"צהריים","en":"noon","alt":["lunch"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"arukhat"},{"he":"אוכלות","en":"eating","alt":["are eating","eat"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"okhelet"},{"he":"הפירות","en":"the fruit","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"הבשר","en":"the meat","alt":["the flesh"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"מלח","en":"salt","alt":[],"from":"lexicon","tr":"melakh"},{"he":"כריך","en":"sandwich","alt":["a sandwich"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"karikh"},{"he":"ארוחת צהריים","en":"lunch","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"arukhat"},{"he":"ארוחת ערב","en":"dinner","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"arukhat"},{"he":"ארוחת בוקר","en":"breakfast","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"arukhat"},{"he":"הזיתים","en":"Mount of olives","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"har"},{"he":"אננס","en":"pineapple","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"ananas"},{"he":"זיתים","en":"olive","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"zayit"},{"he":"רוצות","en":"want (feminine plural)","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"rotzot"},{"he":"הקפה","en":"the coffee","alt":["the coffee is"],"from":"skill"},{"he":"בקר","en":"beef","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"bakar"},{"he":"דג","en":"fish","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"dag"},{"he":"קפה","en":"coffee","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"kafeh"},{"he":"מרק","en":"soup","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"marak"},{"he":"פטרייה","en":"mushroom","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"pitriyah"},{"he":"פיצה","en":"pizza","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"pitzah"},{"he":"סלט","en":"salad","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"salat"},{"he":"רוצֶה","en":"wants","alt":["want","would like"],"from":"phrase","tr":"rotzeh"},{"he":"את","en":"you","alt":["the fruit"],"from":"phrase","tr":"at"},{"he":"טעים","en":"tasty","alt":["delicious"],"from":"phrase","tr":"ta'im"},{"he":"תודה","en":"thanks","alt":["thank you"],"from":"phrase","tr":"todah"},{"he":"אני","en":"I","alt":["I am","me"],"from":"phrase","tr":"ani"},{"he":"אנחנו","en":"we","alt":["we are"],"from":"phrase","tr":"anakhnu"},{"he":"והם","en":"and they(masculine)","alt":["and they are(masculine)"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"לחם","en":"bread","alt":[],"from":"phrase","tr":"lekhem"}],"lexemes":["ארוחת צהריים","ארוחת ערב","ארוחת בוקר","כריך","הזיתים","אננס","זיתים","רוצות","הקפה","הפטרייה","בקר","דג","וקפה","קפה","מרק","הדג","פטרייה","הפיצה","הסלט","רוצים","פיצה","סלט","המרק","הבקר"],"tips":"**The accusative**\n--------------\nWhen an action is being done to a noun, we call that noun \"the direct object\".\n\nYou will remember from Letters 1 that there is no indefinite article (\"a\"/\"an\") in Hebrew, and that in order to add a definite article (\"the\") to a noun we simply connect the letter ה to the noun.\n\nHowever, when that noun is the *direct object* of the sentence, we also need to add another word before it. This word has no English equivalent or translation, and all it does is it tells you that the noun which is about to follow is the direct object. For now you only need to use it with the definite article, ה. If you find words like \"definite\", \"article\" and \"direct\" confusing, don't worry! Duolingo is designed to help you understand when to use words like את through practice. \n\nTry not to confuse את *et*, with the identically-spelled את *at*. You can tell which pronunciation to use from the context. (See the example at the bottom of this page)\n\nExamples using את *et*:\n\nילד אוכל תפוח - A boy eats an apple.\n\n**ה**ילד אוכל תפוח - **The** boy eats an apple.\n\nילד אוכל ***את ה***תפוח - A boy eats ***the*** apple.\n\n**ה**ילד אוכל ***את ה***תפוח - **The** boy eats ***the*** apple.\n\nIf the direct object is a name, then את is still required, but we don't add ה:  \nהילד אוכל את יוסי  \nThe boy eats Yossi!\n\n*et* vs *at*\n-----------------\nYou can usually tell from the context whether את is to be pronounced as \"et\" or \"at\":\n\nאת אוכלת את התפוח - You (f) eat the apple. **at** okhélet **et** hatapúakh\n\nThe first את is followed by a verb (a \"doing word\"), so it has to be *at*, \"you\". The second is followed by ה + a noun which is **receiving** the action (it is **being eaten**), so it is *et*."}